Key mental model
Git has three areas:

text
working tree   →   staging area (index)   →   repository (.git)
        git add                    git commit


And four kinds of "undo" you must not confuse:
restore — discard changes
reset — move HEAD / unstage
revert — make an inverse commit
reflog — the time machine when all else fails
Memorize git status, git log --oneline, git add -p, git commit --amend, git reflog and you'll be dangerous in a good way.






